        ":question/id": "ec9f81d0-f152-5c1c-b7c8-fd08eb67e7c0",
        ":question/problem": "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\u2207f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
