        ":question/problem": "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-2y).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\u2207f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-2y)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x-2y)) \\\\  & =-2{sec}^{2}\u2061(x-2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}\u2061(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}\u2061(x-2y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
