        ":question/worked-solution": "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\\nabla f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(\\ln{\\left(2 x + 6 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{2 x + 6 y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\ln{\\left(2 x + 6 y \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{6}{2 x + 6 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y)&=f_{x}(x,y)\\,i+f_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{2 x + 6 y}\\,i+\\frac{6}{2 x + 6 y}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
